        },
        {
            "summary": "Stoppage in Transitu and Its Application",
            "explanation": "Stoppage in transitu (途中停运权) is a legal term indicating that an unpaid seller can regain possession of goods during transportation if the buyer becomes insolvent, until payment or tender of the price is made. This right allows sellers to detain goods during transport after parting with their physical possession when the buyer becomes insolvent and the property has passed to them (途中的停运权). The term 'stoppage in transitu' refers to a legal right where an unpaid seller can regain possession and retain goods during transportation if the buyer becomes insolvent, until payment or tender of the price is made. This event can significantly impact logistics operations as it involves detaining goods mid-transportation."
        },
        {
            "summary": "Insolvency and Its Impact",
            "explanation": "Insolvency (无力偿债) refers to a situation where an entity cannot pay its debts, which can trigger the seller's right to retain possession of the goods. This legal concept is crucial in understanding how unpaid seller’s lien operates when buyers become unable to meet their financial obligations. Insolvency is both a financial event and a legal condition that allows sellers to exercise their rights over goods sold on credit or without stipulated payment terms (无力偿债是指一个实体无法支付其债务；它既是财务事件也是法律概念)。"
        },
